From 352549eb1aec7a9f1becf0ec77ae43ea3f6cb614 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: duck-brain <duck-brain@localhost>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 00:07:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] duck-brain P12: the body IMU on the host's I2C
 (`[body_imu]`)

On the duck-brain robot the LSM6DSV16X sits on the Zero 3W's own I2C,
not on an imu_to_dxl board on the servo bus.

- robotd/src/body_imu.rs: a reader thread polls the chip at
  `[body_imu] poll_hz` (default 200, at least 100). Bring-up is
  head_imu's (imu_to_dxl's: reset, reload trimming, configure, read back,
  SFLP), batching gyro, accel and the game quaternion at 120 Hz (FIFO_CTRL3
  0x66, SFLP_ODR 011, checked against ST's lsm6dsv16x_reg.h). FIFO
  records are packed into the imu_to_dxl 12-byte block (raw gyro counts +
  quaternion halves) and decoded by the same SflpDecoder, with its median
  filter off (SflpDecoder::unfiltered). Each sample is stamped and handed
  to the tick through ImuFeed; the tick reports the age of the one it used.
  No magnetometer: heading is the game quaternion's yaw (integrated gyro).
- head_imu.rs: Chip, the register constants and the bring-up rate made
  reachable (Rate::Hz60 for the head as before, Rate::Hz120 for the body).
- [body_imu] params: bus (/dev/i2c-3), address (0x6a or 0x6b), poll_hz,
  mount quaternion (identity until measured); on by default with the
  feetech driver.
- `robotd body-imu [--solve]`: the reader alone, printing gravity, gyro
  and sample age in the trunk frame; --solve measures the mount from two
  still poses (upright, nose-down) and prints [body_imu.mount].
- robot.health `host_imu`: device, error, ready, poll and sample rates.
